From: Ash Pera <ashley.pera@noaa.gov>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 21:37:31 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 06/13] Implement config_positive_definite for scalar transport

config_positive_definite has been in the Registry, but
mpas_atm_dynamics_checks reported it as unimplemented, and
advance_scalars ran the monotonic transport when it was set. A user who
turns the monotonic limiter off has no positive-definite choice. The
unlimited scheme leaves negative mixing ratios, and atm_srk3 then zeroes
them before the physics, which adds mass.

Measured on the idealized supercell (84x84 doubly periodic mesh, dx = 2 km,
dt = 12 s, Thompson microphysics with its water fixes, no surface fluxes,
double precision, 2 h, config_monotonic = false): domain water plus
precipitation gains 1.40 kg/m2, 0.69 of the precipitation. All of it comes
from that zeroing.

Implementation:
- With config_positive_definite = true and config_monotonic = false, the
  final RK stage uses positive-definite flux renormalization (Skamarock
  2006, MWR 134, 2241-2250; WRF's moist_adv_opt = 1).
- Where a cell's total outgoing high-order flux in the step exceeds its
  content, the fluxes leaving it are scaled to its content.
- Each face takes its donor cell's factor, so the update is conservative.
  Incoming fluxes are not limited.
- It reuses the monotonic routine with no low-order part: the full flux
  takes the place of the antidiffusive one. The factor goes into SCALE_OUT
  (SCALE_IN = 1), and the existing halo exchange of the scale factors
  makes it consistent across tasks.
- Where no cell's outflow exceeds its content, the fluxes are unchanged.
- With config_monotonic = true the monotonic transport is used, as before.
  It is also positive definite.
- The option is not available with lateral boundary conditions; the
  monotonic transport is used then.
- mpas_atm_dynamics_checks now says which of these applies.

Unit tests of atm_pd_factor, extracted verbatim, applied with MPAS's
rescale formula to third-order fluxes on a 2-D x-z periodic slab:
- At (horizontal, vertical) Courant numbers from (0.3, 0.5) to (1.5, 3.0),
  the unlimited update leaves values down to -6.2e-3 (q ~ 1e-3 kg/kg).
  With the renormalization the minimum is -3.3e-19, which is roundoff, and
  mass is conserved to 4e-15.
- 19,612 slabs in which no outflow exceeds the content were unchanged, bit
  for bit.

Staged, not yet run on the supercell: config_monotonic = false with
config_positive_definite = true, where I expect the domain closure at
roundoff.

AI-assisted: written with Claude Code (Anthropic); reviewed by the author.
